# SatEngine Architecture

SatEngine is a C++20 game engine (CMake + GLFW). Prefer small, focused changes that match the existing layout.

## Layout

- `Engine/` — reusable static library target `SatEngine`
  - `Core/` — application loop, window, core types (`include/`, `src/`)
  - `Platform/` — OS / input / platform backends
  - `Renderer/` — graphics API wrappers and render systems
    - `include/` — public D3D-free API (`Renderer.hpp`, `SceneDraw.hpp`, …)
    - `src/` — thin facade (`Renderer.cpp`)
    - `src/module/` — private session, render passes, and GPU helpers (`RenderSession`, `MeshPass`, …)
  - `Assets/` — engine-owned assets and loaders
  - `UI/` — editor / ImGui layer (`include/`, `src/`)
- `GamePlayer/` — standalone game player executable; links `SatRuntime`
- `scripts/` — build helpers
- `build/` — generated; never edit

## Module folder (`src/module/`)

Use `Engine/<Area>/src/module/` for focused implementation units that are **not** public API (e.g. `MeshPass`, `SelectionOutlinePass`, `TranslateGizmoPass`).

- Keep each module’s `.hpp` next to its `.cpp` under `src/module/` — do **not** put these headers in `include/`
- Third-party / graphics API types (D3D11, etc.) may appear only in `src/` and `src/module/`
- The area facade (e.g. `Renderer`, `UiLayer`) stays thin, includes its session as `"module/Foo.hpp"`, and delegates orchestration there
- Other engine areas follow the same pattern when they grow internal multi-file subsystems

## Boundaries

- Engine must never depend on `GamePlayer/`
- Public API lives in `Engine/*/include/`; implementation in `src/` (and `src/module/`)
- Hide third-party types (GLFW, ImGui, D3D) behind engine wrappers / PIMPL
- Register every new engine `.cpp` in `Engine/CMakeLists.txt`
- Keep `GamePlayer/` thin: startup and embedded project host only

## Ownership

- `Application` owns the main loop and top-level systems
- Non-copyable types own resources; transfer with move or unique ownership only
